This thing also carries an additional benefit: For each organization, there is only 1 peer that connects to the ordering service, and it receives blocks in-order. 
If that peer doesn't have the ledger of the channel (because it is not part of the channel), but it has the MSP because it was replicated to it, it could verify the signatures on the blocks it gets from the ordering service. 

