  // blank if the query is returning information about installed chaincodes.
  string escc = 5;
  // the name of the VSCC for this chaincode. This will be
  // blank if the query is returning information about installed chaincodes.
  string vscc = 6;
}
{code}

Once this is done, this will need to be exposed on the SDK.  $acceptance criteria:$

description:
This query should provide the names of all the channels a given peer has joined.

The query can be called from CLI as follows: 

{code}
peer chaincode invoke -C testchainid -n cscc -c '{"Args":["GetChannels"]}'
{code}

The query will return a ChannelQueryResponse proto with the following definition:
{code}
// ChannelQueryResponse returns information about each channel that pertains
// to a query in lccc.go, such as GetChannels (returns all channels for a
// given peer)
message ChannelQueryResponse {
  repeated ChannelInfo channels = 1;
}

// ChannelInfo contains general information about channels
message ChannelInfo {
  string channel_id = 1;
}
{code}

Once this is done, this will need to be exposed on the SDK.

